SOAPBOX: Since my shack is under renovation, I used my backup daily driver - my classic Kenwood TS-940SAT - purchased used in 1995 from the original owner. It was stored for nearly a decade before I got the chance to finish a refurb, and update the rig, about 3 years ago. it is now part of my backup shack.
SOAPBOX: I was really thrilled by the massive openings to EU on 10 & 15 meters both mornings - and lots of JAs too.
SOAPBOX: Signals were clean and clear with no QSB, and my barefoot signals to the 31 foot wire vertical were heard, with little need for repeats. I worked S&P exclusively, and DX exclusively. Thanks to all for the great QSOs.
SOAPBOX: 73 de W6JBR
